W: 2. O they ploughed him in the furrow deep
W: Till the clods lay o'er his head
W: And these three men were rejoicing then
W: John Barleycorn was dead
W: [Chorus:]
W:
W: 3. Ihey left him there for a week or so
W: And a shower of rain did fall
W: John Barleycorn sprung up again
W: And he proved them liars all
W: [Chorus:]
W:
W: 4. Then they hired men with sickles
W: To cut him off at the knee
W: And the worst of all they served Barleycorn
W: They served him barbarously
W: [Chorus:]
W:
W: 5. Then they hired men with pitchforks
W: To pitch him onto the load
W: And the worst of all they served Barleycorn
W: They bound him down with cord
W: [Chorus:]
W:
W: 6. Then they hired men with thrashels
W: To beat him high and low
W: Ihey came smick-smack on poor Jack's back
W: Till the flesh bled every blow
W: [Chorus:]
W:
W: 7. O the next they put him in the maltin' kiln
W: Thinking to dry his bones
W: And the worst of all they served Barleycorn
W: They crushed him between two stones
W: [Chorus:]
W:
W: 8. Then they put him into the mashing-tub
W: Ihinking to scald his tail
W: And the next thing they called Barleycorn
W: Ihey called him home-brewed ale
W: [Chorus:]
W:
W: 9. So come put your wine into glasses
W: Your cider in tin-cans
W: But young Barleycorn in the old brown jug
W: For he proves the strongest man
W: [Chorus:]
%
